Github repository for Red Pitaya data aqcuisition for use as SDR.
Edie Simecek

Link to Red Pitaya Getting Started: 
https://docs.google.com/document/d/19OnYhg5kkh0p6dgTRoniobef44eeiYhupY4dir2BS4U/edit?pli=1&tab=t.0

There are multiple ways to stream data on the red pitaya:

-on red pitaya UI
    type rp-xxxxxx.local into search bar. click on streaming application or any others necessary

-over scpi server
    create program using red pitaya's scpi library
    start scpi server on UI or in terminal. Then run program

-red pitaya api
    copy programs written in red pitaya's api to red pitaya
    ssh into the red pitaya and run programs directly on the machine

-automation scripts for api programs
    skip copying and sshing into the red pitaya with Edie's automation scripts for cpp and py

-Pavel Denim's projects
    requires exploration

Contents of Repository:

-rp_acquisition
    programs to receive a signal using the red pitaya. 

-data
    raw data files captured my red pitaya

-plots
    plots created from raw data

-plotter
    programs to plot raw data files (depending on data format)

-automated ssh
    automated scripts to expedite copying and ssh

-feedbackloop
    programs for a simple hello world feedback loop. Check to make sure rp can generate and acquire data correctly

-fpga
    coherent integration program for raw radio data acquisition and preliminary processing


**All cpp files can be compiled with the Makefile found within automated ssh**
